  {
    "id": "3818647919",
    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "F1 Pit Wall - Live Standings, Countdown & Session Results",
    "description": "F1 PIT WALL — Live Formula 1 dashboard for your desktop\n\nEverything you need for the race weekend at a glance, fully automatic.\n\nFEATURES\n• Big clock + date\n• Countdown to the next session (FP1, FP2, FP3, Sprint Quali, Sprint, Qualifying, Race) — all times shown in YOUR local time zone\n• \"LIVE\" indicator with elapsed time while a session is running, glowing panel 15 min before a session starts\n• Top 8 after every session: as soon as Practice 1 ends, the result panel switches to the Practice 1 top 8 (best lap + gaps), then Practice 2, Practice 3, Qualifying, Sprint … After the race it shows the race result (top 10)\n• Drivers' and constructors' standings with team colours and gaps to the leader\n• Track weather for Fri/Sat/Sun of the race weekend (temperature + rain chance) and the local time at the circuit\n• Title fight: points still available, who can still mathematically win the title, and the earliest race the leader can clinch it\n• Season progress bar (races completed)\n\nHOW IT UPDATES\n• Standings, schedule and results refresh every 10 minutes\n• Session results (top 8) are checked automatically after every session — usually available a few minutes after the chequered flag\n• Weather refreshes every hour\n• If you're offline it keeps showing the last saved data\n• No account, no API key, nothing to set up\n\nSETTINGS\n• Accent colour\n• Highlight a driver (enter the 3-letter code, e.g. VER, LEC, NOR — leave empty for none)\n• Layout: Full or Minimal (clock + countdown only — great for a second monitor)\n• Show/hide seconds\n• Optional animated speed lines\n• Custom background image (automatically dimmed so everything stays readable)\n\nPERFORMANCE\nLightweight: no constant animations by default, only the numbers that change get redrawn. Wallpaper Engine pauses it automatically while you're in a fullscreen game.\n\nDesigned for 1920×1080, scales to any 16:9 resolution.\n\nDATA SOURCES\nJolpica F1 (schedule, standings, results), OpenF1 (session results), Open-Meteo (weather).\n\nUnofficial fan project. Not affiliated with Formula 1, the FIA or any team.",
